  "prompt": "Use case: precise native game-map repair with physical plank joinery. Return exactly ONE opaque1254x1254 image with the same framing as Image1. Repair ONLY the floor rectangle x338..858,y406..1024. Across the internal vertical join x512, the narrow floor planks arriving from LEFT have different spacing/count from the broader floor planks on RIGHT. Do not force each long groove to continue into a different-height groove. Instead reconcile the two plank fields using 2 or 3 natural staggered short butt joints and T-junctions between individual wood boards. Keep the left narrow board field and right broad board field at their existing positions. Use short diagonal board-END seams in the opposite isometric direction to the long diagonal grooves: ends slope up-right, approximately from lower-left to upper-right. A broad right-hand board may meet the ends of two narrow left-hand boards. Stagger these joints at varied x positions inside the rectangle, with no full vertical stack and no cover strip. Indicative end-joint regions are around x430..650,y540..650; x380..650,y700..820; x490..780,y860..980, but fit actual surrounding native endpoints precisely rather than tracing these coordinates. The result MUST visibly contain plausible staggered plank ends/T joints, not a globally straightened floor. Every groove reaching x338 or x858 or y406 or y1024 must meet the immutable native groove just outside without a step. Keep all pixels outside the rectangle unchanged: upper railing, large post base, sea, nails, knots, plank endpoints and all shadows there are fixed. Preserve the shadow inside the rectangle continuously. Match existing warm amber hand-painted wood, fine grain, original scale and soft rounded Daoist Q style. No new beam, additional post, boat, object, text, border or watermark. One1254square.",
